   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law and the executive law, in relation\nto enabling veterans and reservists to receive benefit information upon\napplying for or renewing a driver's license",
    "basePrintNo": "S6452",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6452-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 5,
       "fullName": "Jim Gaughran",
       "imgName": "1042_Jim_Gaughran.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1222,
       "sessionMemberId": 1807,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "GAUGHRAN"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §508, V & T L; amd §354-a, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6452\n\nSPONSOR: REICHLIN-MELNICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law and the executive law, in\nrelation to enabling veterans and reservists to receive benefit informa-\ntion upon applying for or renewing a driver's license\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nEnables veterans or reservists to receive benefit information upon\nrequesting and obtaining a notation upon a license or non-driver iden-\ntification card that he or she is a veteran.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 508 of the vehicle and traffic law to require\nthe commissioner of the Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV) to consult\nwith the director of the Division of Veterans' Services (DVS) to estab-\nlish a process by which the DMV shall refer any driver's license and\nnon-driver identification card applicant who requests and receives a\nnotation upon such license or non-driver identification card that he or\nshe is a veteran.\n\nSection 2 amends section 354-a of the executive law to require any indi-\nvidual requesting and obtaining a veterans notation on their driver's\nlicense or non-driver identification card to be advised of DVS's and\nlocal veterans' service agencies provide assistance to veterans regard-\ning benefits under federal and state law.\n\nSection 3 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would help veterans who seek a veterans notation on a\ndriver's license or non-driver identification card to receive informa-\ntion about benefits that they may be entitled to under federal and state\nlaw.. At no cost to taxpayers, this bill utilizes the DMV as an intake\npoint to gather information on veterans not currently in the state\nsystem.\n\nMany men and women who have bravely served our country are often unaware\nor unsure of certain benefits that are available to them.  This bill\nwould help ensure DVA receives their information and then ultimately\nhelp more veterans receive their much deserved benefits.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: S.1026 - Passed Senate\n\n2015-16: S.775A - Passed Senate\n\n2013-14: S.2226-B - Passed Senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThere are no fiscal implications associated with the passage of this\nlegislation.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the 180th day after it shall have become a\nlaw. Effective immediately, the addition, amendment and/or repeal of any\nrule or regulation necessary for the implementation of this act on its\neffective date are authorized to be made and completed on or before such\neffective date.\n",
